Data Types
│
├── Primitive
│   ├── Floating Point
│   │   ├── float (4 Bytes → 32 bits → IEEE 754) --> Range of float(Approx range) --> +/- 3.4 × 10^38 to +/- 1.2 × 10^-38

Value = (-1)^sign × 1.mantissa × 2^(exponent - bias)

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bit Position:  31 | 30 .......... 23 | 22 ....................... 0
               -----------------------------------------------------
Field:         Sign |   Exponent   |        Mantissa (Fraction)
Bits Count:     1   |      8       |             23

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Bit:   31   30 29 28 27 26 25 24 23   22 ................. 0
       -----------------------------------------------------
       S    E  E  E  E  E  E  E  E    M  M  M  M  M ...    M
       
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Internally:
When you write:
    float x = 10.25
    Compiler converts → IEEE 754 format
Stored as:
    * 01000001001001000000000000000000
    * CPU reads:
        * sign
        * exponent
        * mantissa
    * Reconstructs value using formula
    * When printing:
        * Converted back → decimal (10.25)


Binary conversion
10 → 1010
0.25 → 0.01

Normalization
So:
10.25 = 1010.01

1010.01 = 1.01001 × 2^3
sign | Exponent | Mantissa   
0    | 10000010 | 01001000000000000000000  
    
Fill IEEE Fields
    1bit             8bits                          23bits
    1. Sign bit      2. Exponent                    3. Mantissa (remove leading 1)
    0 (positive)        Bias = 127                     01001 (rest padded to 23 bits)
                        Exponent = 3 + 127 = 130       01001000000000000000000
                        Binary = 10000010
    
